{"series":{"id":"cost-of-living::median-gross-rent-income-percent","label":"Median gross rent as % of household income","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"percent of renter household income","scope":"us_states","definition":"Published ACS B25071_E001 median gross rent as a percentage of household income; B25071_M001 is the published 90% margin in percentage points. This direct published household-ratio median is not annualized median rent divided by median household income.","denominator":"Renter-occupied housing units paying cash rent, as defined by Census; percentage of each household’s income","reporting_period":"2024 ACS 1-year estimate","source_url":"https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/summary_file/2024/table-based-SF/data/1YRData/acsdt1y2024-b25071.dat","sources":[{"id":"acs-rent-burden-2024","title":"U.S. Census · ACS 2024 B25071 median gross rent as a share of household income","url":"https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/summary_file/2024/table-based-SF/data/1YRData/acsdt1y2024-b25071.dat","date":"2024 ACS 1-year estimates; retrieved 2026-10-28","note":"Direct published median gross-rent percentage of household income, for renter-occupied housing units paying cash rent. This is not a ratio calculated from two unrelated medians. MOE is in percentage points.","license":"U.S. federal government public information; source attribution retained."}],"limitations":["RPP compares state price levels within a given year. It is not a year-to-year inflation rate, a complete family living budget or a required-income estimate.","All-items U.S. RPP is 100, while published U.S. component rows are not all exactly 100. The original indexes and each actual national component reference are preserved without renormalization.","Housing-services RPP reflects rents, including how rental evidence supports the accounts; it is not a home-purchase-price index. ACS gross rent is monthly rent plus estimated tenant-paid utilities/fuels.","ACS B25071 directly publishes the